{
  "_about": "laneDIRPROOF v1: thresholds and move rows of the directed-input proof driver (DirProof.cs, harness arg -dirproof:<names>). Nothing here is read without the arg. kind: attack | guard | parry | dodge | hitreact. Every row is selected by its name in the -dirproof list. attack: dir = attack.sectors name fed through controls.json attack.map (the same move pick as DirectionalInput.MoveFor); heavy true = the heavy list; expectDirs = MoveDef.direction values accepted; allowResults = contact types that count as a landed result; reactStates = foe states accepted as a hit reaction (empty = not checked). guard: side = guard.sides name or alias (centre aliases = side id 0); the verdict is judged per contact the foe makes while the guard is up (covers true must be Blocked/Parried, covers false must be Hit/GuardBroken). parry: raise the guard (side = best cover of the foe's swing) when the foe wind-up has raiseWhenWindupLeftTicks left. dodge: press = roll | backstep | sidestepL | sidestepR. hitreact: guard down, wait for a hit on Joan.",
